  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, who claims to have psychic abilities and is the daughter of a long-reigning European monarch, married Durek Verrett, an American who identifies as a sixth-generation shaman, on Saturday afternoon. Despite the unconventional nature of this royal wedding, onlookers gathered along the cloudy streets of Geiranger hoping to see the bride. The 52-year-old princess, who is fourth in the line of succession to the Norwegian throne and the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, wed the 49-year-old Verrett in a Church of Norway ceremony. The event took place at the Hotel Union, a four-star establishment located in a small village under the Geiranger fjord, and was attended by both royal family members and famous personalities. Seven bridesmaids accompanied the princess, including her two teenage daughters, Leah and Emma Behn, from her previous marriage to Norwegian writer Ari Behn, who passed away after their 2017 divorce. The guest list of approximately 350 people included her brother Crown Prince Haakon and his spouse Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Sweden's Crown Princess Victoria with her husband Prince Daniel, and Prince Constantijn along with Princess Laurentien from the Netherlands. Princess Märtha Louise has led an unorthodox royal existence, having previously proclaimed herself to have clairvoyant powers and operated a healing institution for ten years where she instructed students in communicating with angels. In 2022, she declared she would resign from her official royal responsibilities to concentrate on the business ventures she shares with Verrett and to create a clearer separation between their commercial activities and Norway's royal family. On Instagram, Verrett identifies himself as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator,' with Gwyneth Paltrow, the founder of Goop, among his prominent clients, whom he refers to as a 'soul sister.'"
